wq('2',1,'A cargo box that may slide or tip','A.2',r'''A rigid box of mass $6.00\,\mathrm{kg}$ has a rectangular cross section $0.80\,\mathrm m$ by $0.40\,\mathrm m$ and its centre of mass at the geometric centre. The horizontal floor has $\mu_s=0.50$ and $\mu_k=0.30$. Use $g=9.81\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-2}}$.

First the box rests on its $0.80\,\mathrm m$ wide base. A horizontal $35.0\,\mathrm N$ force acts through its centre and moves it $1.20\,\mathrm m$ from rest. The force is removed and the box slides to rest.

In a second experiment the box rests upright on its $0.40\,\mathrm m$ wide base. A slowly increasing horizontal force is applied at height $0.80\,\mathrm m$.''',[
('a',r'Calculate the maximum static friction and explain why motion begins in the first experiment.',2),
('b',r'Determine the speed when the force is removed and the further distance before the box stops.',3),
('c',r'Determine whether the upright box slides or tips first, and calculate the corresponding applied-force threshold.',3),
('d',r'For the upright box, determine the application height at which sliding and tipping thresholds coincide.',2)
],[('a',[('A1',r'$F_{s,max}=\mu_smg=29.43\,\mathrm N$.'),('R1',r'The applied $35.0\,\mathrm N$ exceeds this threshold, so static friction cannot maintain equilibrium; the centre-height force does not overturn the wide box first.')]),
('b',[('M1',r'$F_k=17.658\,\mathrm N$ and work-energy gives $\tfrac12mv^2=(35.0-17.658)(1.20)$.'),('A1',r'$v=2.63378\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}\approx2.63\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$.'),('A1',r'After release, $F_kd=\tfrac12mv^2$, giving $d=1.17853\,\mathrm m\approx1.18\,\mathrm m$.')]),
('c',[('M1',r'At incipient tipping about the downstream lower corner, $F(0.80)=mg(0.20)$.'),('A1',r'$F_{tip}=14.715\,\mathrm N\approx14.7\,\mathrm N$.'),('R1',r'This is less than the sliding threshold $29.43\,\mathrm N$, so the upright box tips first. Static friction at this force is below its limiting value.')]),
('d',[('M1',r'Set $mg(0.20)/H=\mu_smg$.'),('A1',r'$H=0.20/0.50=0.400\,\mathrm m$. A lower push produces sliding first; a higher push produces tipping first.')])],
[src(1,'1a-c','Friction and a finite push followed by free sliding','1.pdf'),src(2,'1d','Competition between sliding and overturning','1.pdf')],fig,'ahl',['A.2','A.3','A.4'])

