wq('2',2,'A moving optical relay and separated emissions','A.5',r'''Two laboratory beacons lie at $x=0$ and $x=900\,\mathrm m$. The left beacon emits event $A$ at $t=0$; the right emits event $B$ at $t=1.50\,\mathrm{\mu s}$. A relay moves along $+x$ at $0.600c$, passing $x=0$ at $A$. Laboratory and relay clocks are zero at $A$. Use $c=3.00\times10^8\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$.

The diagram shows the relay worldline (solid) and the left-going light pulse emitted at $B$ (dashed). In the relay frame use $\Delta x\prime=\gamma(\Delta x-v\Delta t)$ and $\Delta t\prime=\gamma(\Delta t-v\Delta x/c^2)$.''',[
('a',r'Calculate $\Delta x\prime$ and $\Delta t\prime$ between emissions $A$ and $B$.',3),
('b',r'Explain the order of the emissions in the relay frame and whether either emission could cause the other.',2),
('c',r'Keeping the beacon positions fixed, determine the laboratory time of $B$ that would make the two emissions simultaneous in the relay frame.',2),
('d',r'For the original emission times, determine the relay-clock reading when it receives the pulse from the right beacon.',3)
],[('a',[('A1',r'$\gamma=1/\sqrt{1-0.600^2}=1.25$.'),('A1',r'$\Delta x\prime=1.25(900-0.600\times450)=787.5\,\mathrm m$.'),('A1',r'$\Delta t\prime=1.25(1.50-1.80)=-0.375\,\mathrm{\mu s}$.')]),
('b',[('R1',r'Because $\Delta t\prime<0$, the relay assigns $B$ before $A$.'),('R1',r'The interval is spacelike: $(c\Delta t)^2-(\Delta x)^2=450^2-900^2<0$. No light or slower signal can connect the two emissions, so reversing their coordinate order violates no causality.')]),
('c',[('M1',r'Simultaneity requires $\Delta t=v\Delta x/c^2$.'),('A1',r'$t_B=0.600(900)/c=1.80\,\mathrm{\mu s}$ after $A$ in the laboratory.')]),
('d',[('M1',r'The relay has $x=0.600ct$ and the incoming pulse has $x=900-c(t-1.50\times10^{-6})$.'),('M1',r'Equating gives $t=2.8125\,\mathrm{\mu s}$ and $x=506.25\,\mathrm m$ in the laboratory.'),('A1',r'The relay proper time from $A$ is $t/\gamma=2.25\,\mathrm{\mu s}$.')])],
[src(3,'2a-b','Spacetime worldlines and moving-frame light reception','1.pdf'),src(4,'2c-d','Simultaneity and frame-dependent measurements','1.pdf')],fig,'ahl')

