wq('2',3,'A rectangular heat-engine cycle','B.4',r'''A closed sample of monatomic ideal gas follows $A\to B\to C\to D\to A$ on the diagram, quasi-statically along each straight segment. It takes in heat from a $1000\,\mathrm K$ reservoir during $AB$ and $BC$, and rejects heat to a $100\,\mathrm K$ reservoir during $CD$ and $DA$. Its amount is $0.200\,\mathrm{mol}$ and $R=8.31\,\mathrm{J\,mol^{-1}\,K^{-1}}$. Use $U=3pV/2$ and the convention $Q=\Delta U+W$, with $W$ positive for work by the gas.''',[
('a',r'Determine the net work by the gas in one cycle and relate its sign to the cycle direction.',2),
('b',r'Calculate the total heat absorbed from the hot reservoir in one cycle.',3),
('c',r'Find the efficiency and compare it with the Carnot limit for the stated reservoirs.',2),
('d',r'Calculate the total entropy change of the gas plus both reservoirs in one cycle. Explain the physical meaning of its sign.',3)
],[('a',[('M1',r'The clockwise cycle encloses $\Delta p\Delta V=(2.00\times10^5)(3.00\times10^{-3})$.'),('A1',r'$W_{cycle}=+600\,\mathrm J$; expansion at high pressure does more work than compression at low pressure.')]),
('b',[('M1',r'Along $AB$, $W=0$ and $Q_{AB}=\tfrac32V_A(p_B-p_A)=600\,\mathrm J$.'),('M1',r'Along $BC$, $Q=\Delta U+p\Delta V=(\tfrac32+1)p_B(V_C-V_B)=2250\,\mathrm J$.'),('A1',r'$Q_{in}=2850\,\mathrm J$.')]),
('c',[('A1',r'$\eta=W/Q_{in}=600/2850=0.210526\approx21.1\%$.'),('R1',r'The Carnot bound is $1-100/1000=0.900$, so the calculated efficiency is below it.')]),
('d',[('M1',r'The gas returns to its initial state, so $\Delta S_{gas}=0$. Rejected heat is $Q_{out}=2850-600=2250\,\mathrm J$.'),('M1',r'$\Delta S_{total}=-2850/1000+2250/100=19.65\,\mathrm{J\,K^{-1}}$.'),('R1',r'The positive total entropy change is consistent with an irreversible cycle, including heat transfer across finite temperature differences. Quasi-static gas motion alone does not make the whole process reversible.')])],
[src(5,'3a','Pressure-volume cyclic processes and gas states','1.pdf'),src(6,'3b-c','Work and heat-engine interpretation','1.pdf')],fig,'ahl')

