wq('2',4,'A moving receiver compares two sound beacons','C.5',r'''Two stationary sound beacons $A$ and $B$ lie to the left and right of a moving receiver. The air is stationary. The graph is a spatial snapshot of the wave from $A$, whose period is $2.00\,\mathrm{ms}$. Beacon $B$ emits at $650\,\mathrm{Hz}$. While the receiver moves directly right, its measured frequency ratio is $f_B\prime/f_A\prime=1.80$. The receiver speed is constant and smaller than the sound speed.

The beacons also transmit an optical line of laboratory wavelength $656.0\,\mathrm{nm}$. The receiver spectrometer resolves wavelength differences no smaller than $0.010\,\mathrm{nm}$. Use $c=3.00\times10^8\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$ for light.''',[
('a',r'Use the graph and period to determine the sound speed and beacon $A$ frequency.',2),
('b',r'Determine the receiver speed from the measured sound-frequency ratio.',3),
('c',r'Calculate the two sound frequencies actually received.',2),
('d',r'Estimate the magnitude of the optical wavelength shift caused by this receiver motion. Decide whether the spectrometer can resolve it and explain why the sound shift is much more noticeable.',3)
],[('a',[('A1',r'The wavelength is $0.660\,\mathrm m$, so $v=\lambda/T=0.660/0.00200=330\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$.'),('A1',r'$f_A=1/T=500\,\mathrm{Hz}$.')]),
('b',[('M1',r'The receiver recedes from $A$ and approaches $B$, so $f_A\prime=500(v-u)/v$ and $f_B\prime=650(v+u)/v$.'),('M1',r'$650(330+u)/[500(330-u)]=1.80$.'),('A1',r'$u=53.2258\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}\approx53.2\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$ to the right.')]),
('c',[('A1',r'$f_A\prime=419.355\,\mathrm{Hz}\approx419\,\mathrm{Hz}$.'),('A1',r'$f_B\prime=754.839\,\mathrm{Hz}\approx755\,\mathrm{Hz}$, retaining the ratio $1.80$.')]),
('d',[('M1',r'$|\Delta\lambda|/\lambda\approx u/c=1.77419\times10^{-7}$.'),('A1',r'$|\Delta\lambda|=0.0001164\,\mathrm{nm}$, far below $0.010\,\mathrm{nm}$ and therefore unresolved.'),('R1',r'The dimensionless motion is $u/v\approx0.161$ for sound but only $u/c\approx1.77\times10^{-7}$ for light; the same speed gives very different fractional shifts.')])],
[src(7,'4a-b','Wave spatial and temporal representations','1.pdf'),src(9,'4c(ii)','A moving receiver between stationary beacons','1.pdf'),src(10,'4c(iii)','Small optical Doppler shift','1.pdf')],fig,'ahl',['C.2','C.5'])

